  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: N Emerita Augusta, over R. Albarregas. The\u00a0Albarregas Roman bridge is part of the UNESCO World Heritage site assemblage of Augusta Emerita.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "A Roman bridge with origins in the first century B.C. that crosses the Albarregas River, a tributary of the Guadiana River. The bridge was been declared a Site of Cultural Interest in 1912 and named a part of the UNESCO World Heritage Site \"M\u00e9rida Archaeological Ensemble\" in 1993.",
